        "payload": "tree 2f22c7033245e53315d8a841ec406178f00d764b\nparent a773e1e33b349dc819b5a0edc1c7a4839dc73b48\nauthor Ferdinando Ametrano <ferdinando@ametrano.net> 1792791103 +0200\ncommitter Ferdinando Ametrano <ferdinando@ametrano.net> 1792792375 +0200\n\nvalidation: bound snapshot cache growth by bytes, not coin count\n\nPopulateAndValidateSnapshot checks the coins cache against -dbcache\nonly every 120000 coins. That interval assumes small coins. A coin can\ncarry a script of up to 10000 bytes (MAX_SCRIPT_SIZE), so a snapshot\nfile made of such coins lets the cache grow by about 1.2 GB between two\nchecks, whatever -dbcache is. The file is only rejected at the end,\nwhen the UTXO set hash does not match.\n\nAlso check the cache once its memory usage has grown by 4 MiB since the\nlast check. Typical coins reach this bound about every 30000 coins, so\nthe check runs more often for them too. Reading the usage is a few\nadditions, so the cost is negligible.\n\nAdd a functional test that loads 2000 coins with 10000-byte scripts\nunder -dbcache=4. Without the change the cache is never checked and the\ntest fails. With it the cache is flushed within 5 MiB of its limit.\n",
